As someone mentioned elsewhere, wishes 4-7 (or whatever) aren't nearly as
advantageous as wishes 1 and 2.  Having 3 wishes on DL2, what do you get,
SDSM, speed boots and a cloak of magic resistance?  Then what?  Genocide
scrolls and magic markers, or a tinning kit and a spellbook?  That seems
more making things convenient than particularly less difficult.  Difficulty
is greatly reduced by getting a fountain wish or finding frostbrand two
spaces away from the up staircase on DL1 (happened to me in my only tourist
ascension); is stuff like that tainting?

To a certain degree, I see how it is.  It's probably pretty telling that
the only time I've ascended a tourist I found frostbrand at the beginning
of the game.  But I think mostly wishes beyond the first couple just get
used on luxuries, and it doesn't seem like the extra wishes are really
unbalancing any more than finding nice stuff early is unbalancing.

Plus, if the castle wand in particular had fewer charges, I don't think
anybody who had the inclination to tweak their equipment before descending
further would be any less inclined to do so.  It would just mean that
they'd polypile a lot more.  Which is extremely tedious, and which some of
us can't help doing.  I'd rather just use three wishes on things I want but
don't need than spend an hour and a half standing around Ludios trying to
turn mithril armors into helms of brilliance.  And I'm going to have to do
one or the other.


